==Old English==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|ang|gem-pro|*kattuz}}. Cognate with {{cog|osx|katto}}, {{cog|non|kǫttr}}, {{cog|goh|kazzo}}. A related word also existed in the Germanic languages with the feminine gender, represented in Old English by {{m|ang|catte}}. The word appears to be related to {{cog|LL.|cattus}} as well as to similar words in the Slavic and Celtic languages, but the ultimate source is uncertain. See {{m|en|cat}} for more.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ang-IPA|catt}}

===Noun===
{{ang-noun|m}}

# [[cat]]
#: {{ux|ang|Hēo hrīemþ. Iċ hrīeme. Sē '''catt''' hrīemþ.|She screams. I scream. The '''cat''' screams.}}

